WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Start with one use case and one audience.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.040
Personal productivity, research support, document review, coding, security analysis,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.990
private knowledge search, and workflow automation have different data, quality, latency,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.640
and control requirements.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.405
Describe the job in observable terms.

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:16.030
Instead of build a general assistant,

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.720
define tasks such as summarize approved meeting notes,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.020
answer questions from internal guides with citations,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.400
or draft code changes for human review.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.400
Set boundaries.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.635
Identify data the assistant may access, actions it may take, systems it may call,

00:00:28.635 --> 00:00:31.000
users it may serve, and decisions it must not make.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.875
High-impact actions need stronger review, authorization, and audit.

00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:37.110
Define success before choosing a model.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.920
Measures may include answer correctness, citation support, edit quality, completion rate,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.680
latency, user time saved, privacy compliance, and the cost of mistakes.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.640
Map expected inputs and outputs.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.560
PDFs, markdown, code, images, speech, structured records,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.315
and tool results each change infrastructure and interface needs.

00:00:53.315 --> 00:00:56.907
Sensitive data classifications may prohibit some components or deployments.

00:00:56.907 --> 00:00:59.240
Expand only after the first workflow is reliable.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.680
Adding more documents, users, tools, agents, and automation multiplies failure paths.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.840
A narrow useful assistant earns the evidence needed for a broader one.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.000
Assign a product owner and data owner.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.170
Someone must decide priorities, accept quality, approve sources, handle user reports,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.280
authorize access, and stop a workflow when risk or maintenance exceeds value.
